# img-gen feature plan (higgsfield-style)

## what higgsfield actually offers (from their site research)

### core generation controls
- model picker (nano banana pro, gpt image, seedream, flux, kling o1, soul)
- aspect ratio presets (3:4, 1:1, 16:9, 9:16 etc)
- native 2k / 4k resolution
- upload reference image
- prompt box

### quality / output
- quality tiers (standard / hd)
- native 4k, intelligent refinement
- batch generation (multiple outputs)

### editing / post
- inpaint (brush over area, swap objects, fix bg, change colors)
- image -> video (push to sora 2, kling, seedance)
- upscale (flux 3.0 video upscale, 4k)

### consistency
- soul id: lock character face / identity across generations
- reference image for style / composition

### workflow
- saved configs / presets
- compare outputs side by side
- prompt guide / enhance
- style presets (viral presets)

---

## implementation plan for img-gen

### phase 1 - core api params (done)
- [x] model picker + custom model input
- [x] size / aspect ratio
- [x] count (batch)
- [x] seed
- [x] quality (standard / hd)
- [x] style (vivid / natural)
- [x] negative prompt
- [x] save / load configs (localStorage presets)

### phase 2 - higgsfield-style additions
- [ ] aspect ratio chips (1:1, 3:4, 4:3, 16:9, 9:16) -> map to size
- [ ] resolution tier selector (1k / 2k / 4k) -> map to size or quality
- [ ] reference image upload (base64) -> send to api if supported
- [ ] style presets (photoreal, anime, 3d render, cinematic, etc)
- [ ] prompt enhance toggle (append quality tags)

### phase 3 - advanced
- [ ] inpaint mask editor (canvas brush over uploaded image)
- [ ] image -> video button (push to video api endpoint)
- [ ] soul id / character reference (face lock via reference image + prompt tag)
- [ ] compare mode (side by side grid of last N generations)

### phase 4 - polish
- [ ] generation history (persist to localStorage)
- [ ] download all as zip
- [ ] drag and drop reference image
- [ ] keyboard shortcuts (ctrl+enter, ctrl+s to save config)

---

## notes
- most openai-compatible apis only support model, prompt, n, size, quality, style
- seed, negative_prompt, reference image, inpaint need provider-specific support
- plan is to add UI for all, send only when api supports it
